{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "Scope: The contract requires only patients with complete observed baseline and endpoint data. The analyst imputed missing baseline values (-999) rather than restricting to observed complete cases, thus altering the defined population.",
    "False premise: One of the required premises is that \"Female patients respond better to the treatment than male patients.\" This premise is not verified by the data and, per the contract, should have led to a refusal to answer. The analyst proceeded anyway.",
    "Unacknowledged data problem: The baseline biomarker contains implausible sentinel value -999, indicating systematic missingness. Imputing these values with sex‑specific means may bias the estimated difference, yet the answer presents the point estimate without fully accounting for this limitation."
  ]
}
